Spec: Plugin Registry Service

Purpose:
  Read and update the SpecDD plugin registry while preserving unrelated plugin registrations and resolving their file paths.

Owns:
  ./plugin-registry.ts
  ./plugin-registry.test.ts

References:
  /src/infrastructure/file-system.sdd
  /src/cli-error.sdd

Must:
  Accept @FileSystem and an injectable current-user home directory provider through constructor parameters.
  Locate the registry at `.specdd/plugins.json`, beside the project's bootstrap.
  Treat a missing registry as an empty array without creating it during a read.
  Require the registry to be a JSON array of objects with nonempty string fields `src`, `origin`, `sig`, and `version`.
  Require `sig` to contain exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters representing the SHA-256 of the referenced file's exact bytes.
  Treat `sig` as a content checksum, without interpreting it as a publisher signature.
  Preserve `version` as the supplied version string or `latest` for an installation with no requested version.
  Resolve relative `src` values against the directory containing `plugins.json`, preserve absolute paths, and expand a leading `~` to the current user's home directory.
  Allow resolved source paths outside the project, including paths containing `..`.
  Preserve the original `src` spelling when reading and rewriting existing entries.
  Read registry metadata without requiring unrelated referenced files to exist or match their checksums.
  Reject malformed JSON, invalid entries, and duplicate entries resolving to the same source path before writing.
  Upsert an entry by its resolved source path, retaining its position when replacing and appending when new.
  @pluginRegistrationsMatch compares the exact `src`, `origin`, `sig`, and `version` values, ignoring additional metadata; absent registrations match only other absent registrations.
  @PluginRegistry.upsert accepts an optional expected registration; `null` requires the target to remain absent, while an entry must satisfy @pluginRegistrationsMatch with the registration read for that update; reject a failed precondition without writing.
  Preserve the order and complete values of unrelated entries, including additional fields.
  Write generated entries with `src`, `origin`, `sig`, and `version` string fields and a portable relative `src` using forward slashes.
  Replace registry contents atomically so a failed write leaves the preceding registry intact.

Must not:
  Write plugin files through the paths recorded in registry entries.

Depends on:
  @FileSystem
  Node.js path handling
  Node.js home directory handling

Exposes:
  @PluginRegistry
  @PluginRegistry.read
  @PluginRegistry.resolveSourcePath
  @PluginRegistry.upsert
  @PluginRegistryEntry
  @pluginRegistrationsMatch

Raises:
  @PluginRegistryError extending @CliError for invalid registry data or filesystem failures

Scenario: external source paths
  Given the registry is `/project/.specdd/plugins.json` and the home directory is `/home/alex`
  When sources `../local/plugin.md`, `/shared/plugin.md`, and `~/plugins/plugin.md` are resolved
  Then their paths are `/project/local/plugin.md`, `/shared/plugin.md`, and `/home/alex/plugins/plugin.md`
  And the original registry strings are preserved

Scenario: version metadata changes
  Given a source is registered with version `latest`
  When the same source is upserted with version `v1.2.0` and an unchanged checksum
  Then the existing entry records version `v1.2.0`
  And no duplicate entry is appended

Scenario: malformed registry
  Given an existing entry has no `version` field
  When the registry is read for an installation
  Then a @PluginRegistryError is raised
  And the registry is unchanged

Scenario: conditional update conflicts
  Given an upsert expects the preceding registration
  And that registration has been removed or its source, origin, checksum, or version has changed
  When the registry is updated
  Then a @PluginRegistryError is raised and the current registry bytes are preserved
